          "settings": {
            "heading": "How To Use",
            "icon": "none",
            "heading_size": 16,
            "content": "<p><strong>1. Organize Your Supplies</strong><br/>Pack diapers, wipes, spare clothes, and feeding essentials in the main compartment. Use the smaller pockets for frequently needed items and personal belongings.</p><p><strong>2. Adjust for Comfortable Carrying</strong><br/>Adjust both shoulder straps so the backpack sits evenly against your back. Close all zippers before lifting or carrying the bag.</p><p><strong>3. Unfold the Changing Station</strong><br/>Place the bag on a stable, flat surface at floor level. Open the expandable section and fully extend it according to the included assembly instructions.</p><p><strong>4. Prepare the Changing Area</strong><br/>Lay the changing pad flat and keep diapers, wipes, and clean clothes within reach. Check that all supports are correctly fitted before placing your baby on the pad.</p><p><strong>5. Change Your Baby</strong><br/>Keep your baby within arm’s reach throughout the change. The fold-out section is for supervised diaper changes only, not for sleep or carrying your baby.</p><p><strong>6. Clean and Repack</strong><br/>After moving your baby to a safe place, clean the changing pad according to its care instructions. Allow it to dry completely, then fold the station back into the bag without forcing the supports or zippers.</p>",
